{"a1":[{"k":"title","cap":"Split Into Two Equal Sums","say":"Let's solve Split Into Two Equal Sums, using the Reachable Sums approach.","card":{"title":"Split Into Two Equal Sums","sub":"Reachable Sums · Medium","pattern":"dp"}},{"k":"problem","cap":"Return true if nums (positive integers) can be split into two groups with equal sums.","card":{"lines":["Return true if nums (positive integers) can be split into two groups with equal sums."]}},{"k":"example","cap":"For example, with nums = [1,5,11,5], the answer is true. [1, 5, 5] and [11].","say":"For example, with nums equals 1, 5, 11, 5, the answer is true. 1, 5, 5 and 11.","card":{"lines":["Input: nums = [1,5,11,5]","Output: true","[1, 5, 5] and [11]."]}},{"k":"idea","cap":"If the total is odd it's impossible. Otherwise we need a subset summing to half. Keep the set of sums reachable so far; each number adds itself to every reachable sum.","card":{"pattern":"dp","name":"Dynamic Programming"}},{"k":"trace","cap":"Let's walk through it with nums = [1,5,11,5].","say":"Let's walk through it with nums equals 1, 5, 11, 5.","st":{"vars":[{"k":"target","v":"11"}],"maps":[{"n":"reachable sums","e":[{"k":"0","v":""}]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"With 1, reachable sums are [0].","say":"With 1, reachable sums are 0.","ln":{"python":7,"java":9},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"target","v":"11"}],"maps":[{"n":"reachable sums","e":[{"k":"0","v":""}]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"With 1, reachable sums are [0, 1].","say":"With 1, reachable sums are 0, 1.","ln":{"python":7,"java":9},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"target","v":"11"}],"maps":[{"n":"reachable sums","e":[{"k":"0","v":""},{"k":"1","v":""}]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"With 5, reachable sums are [0, 1].","say":"With 5, reachable sums are 0, 1.","ln":{"python":7,"java":9},"st":{"vars":[{"k":"target","v":"11"}],"maps":[{"n":"reachable sums","e":[{"k":"0","v":""},{"k":"1","v":""}]}]}},{"k":"step","cap":"With 5, reachable sums are [0, 1].","say":"With 5, reachable sums are 0, 1.","ln":{"python":7,"java":9},"st":{"var